+# Philosophy
+
+For whoever proposes a new service, or weighs two good options that no decision record settles. It holds what the
+team favors. Written after the same argument against adding a service was made three times in a year, each time from
+scratch.
+
+## Tenets
+
+### One more service earns its place, or it stays out
+
+Rules out adding a service because it is fast or because one volunteer wants to run it. larder runs one database and
+one web app; a new service must do something Postgres cannot, and two volunteers must be able to restore it, not one.
+This does not rule out every service outside that boundary: a hosted service nobody has to run, such as the card
+gateway, still clears the bar. Applied in [keep sessions in the database](adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)
+and [run background jobs on Postgres](adr/0002-run-background-jobs-on-postgres.md), both turned down a dedicated
+Redis because only one volunteer could restore it.
